 - 2026-06-15: PHASE C2 (HEADLINE confirmation) -- code oracle-distinct replication RETRY on a FRESH second corpus. .393 (exp4246) BLOCKED (blocked_code_second_corpus_missing) -- no distinct cached second code pool was found, so the .392 code win (+3.1pp, single corpus) stays unreplicated. FIX the root cause: GENERATE a fresh second code candidate pool (cached SOTA GGUF best-of-N on MBPP/EvalPlus, per-candidate hidden-test pass labels) if none distinct exists, then run the SAME oracle-distinct gate (learned no-execution pass-predictor over candidate code features + cross-candidate agreement, verifier_is_oracle=false): predictor@1 vs vote@1 vs matched control vs oracle@K, bootstrap CI95-excl-0. Replicates -> the code oracle-distinct win is robust. Honest no-replication (corpus-specific) is COMPLETE. If a fresh pool ALSO cannot be built in-window -> RETIRE the code-replication ask (the .392 +3.1pp stands as a thin single-corpus result). STOP re-running CIRCULAR code-execution selection. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: code_oracle_distinct_replication_corpus_specific; results/experiment_4264_code_oracle_distinct_replication_retry.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE D1 (SOTA-ingestion; mandatory per SOTA-Ingestion Cycle Discipline) -- ingest the SOTA for the .394 bleeding-edge forks (synthesis robustness, discrete-diffusion verifier-guidance, learned-verifier leak/contamination auditing, cross-game ARC transfer) and MAP the strongest 3-5 methods onto the .395 roadmap. Use the RELIABLE channel ONLY (scripts/sweep_clusters.py / sweep_semscholar.py + low-concurrency WebSearch/WebFetch of the top papers) -- the /deep-research harness is BANNED from the autonomous loop. Every method MUST carry a real arXiv ID/URL (no citation = fabrication). Update research-studying.md (mark ingested) and emit flagged_for_v395 (the strongest method conditioned on the .394 A1-A4/B1 outcomes). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: sota_ingestion_v395_mapped; results/experiment_4265_sota_ingestion_v395.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE D2 (hygiene) -- reconcile the verifier registry + gaps to .394 truth, run the GAP-4 regression guard, and LOG missing-verifier gaps. Record the .394 outcomes: the ARC oracle-distinct win's hardened status (survived provenance-blind? replicated multi-seed? transferred cross-game? synthesis broke the ceiling?), the DiffusionGemma preflight GO/NO-GO, the verifier-as-reward out-of-band/retire decision, the code-replication read. Update ops/verifier_registry.yaml + ops/verifier_gaps.md (per Missing-Verifier Gap Logging: any present-but-unselectable ARC failure the set-encoder still misses is a gap entry). Run the GAP-4 execution regression guard (no regression vs .393). Emit regression_guard_passed BARE bool. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: registry_gaps_reconciled_to_v394_truth_regression_guard_passed_True_gaps_logged_4; results/experiment_4266_verifier_registry_gaps_hygiene.json
+- 2026-06-15: PHASE D3 (hardware continuity; opportunistic per north-star §3) -- KV260 terminal/opportunistic (SSH-only reachability + xmutil listapps; NO host SD-card precondition), PolarFire CPU dispatch hash-verify, GateMate USB detect. KV260 is at its terminal state (north-star §3) so the per-board mandate relaxes to opportunistic; this task keeps the boards visible without blocking the milestone. Report per-board reachability + any opportunistic result. NO board blocks the milestone (honest blocked_<board> per board is fine). (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=complete: hardware_continuity_4267_kv260_kv260_terminal_xmutil_listapps_blocked_returncode_1_polarfire_polarfire_hash_verified_cpu_dispatch_succeeded_gatemate_blocked_gatemate_unreachable_ssh_usb_reachability_only; results/experiment_4267_hardware_continuity.json
